        <mxCell id="sample_sort-126" value="All CPUs now have the samples [4, 10, 30]. In practice this means that:&lt;br&gt;- CPU 0 will receive all data below 4&lt;br&gt;- CPU 1 will receive all data from 4 up to 10 (excluded)&lt;br&gt;- CPU 2 will receive all data from 10 up to 30" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=14;spacingLeft=0;" vertex="1" parent="sample_sort-figure">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="540" width="448.3281" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample_sort-127" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 4:&lt;/b&gt; Each CPU sends the portion of its segments to the corresponding CPU, as given by&lt;br&gt;the samples, and sorts the data it receives. As the samples split the range of values in the&lt;br&gt;order of the CPU ranks, the final data is sorted across all CPUs." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=14;spacingLeft=0;" vertex="1" parent="sample_sort-figure">
